# =============================================================================
#  What does NOT go into the repository
# =============================================================================
#  The repository is shared by several people with different search identities.
#  The rule is simple: tools and shared templates go into git; everything
#  personal and everything accumulated does not. See docs/IDENTITIES.md.

# --- Local identities: working copies of templates. Outside git by design —
# --- this is where residency, pay expectations, CVs and everything else a
# --- person is under no obligation to show anyone live. However many folders
# --- are here is how many shortlists the system produces; there is no separate
# --- registry of active identities.
/local-identities/

# --- Accumulated data: the vacancy base, companies, raw dumps, state.
# --- Each user has their own; somebody else's vacancies are useless and only
# --- bloat the repository (~148 MB for the owner). Layout: data/<prefix>/...
/data/

# --- Reports. They sit at the root (they are opened by hand rather than hunted
# --- for in a data tree), but stay out of git for exactly the same reason as
# --- data/: they are the result of one person's search. Layout:
# ---   reports/<prefix>_latest.md
# ---   reports/archive/<prefix>/<date>.md
/reports/

# --- CVs and other personal documents. Their place is inside a local identity
# --- (local-identities/<folder>/documents/), not in the shared repository.
CV *.pdf
CV *.docx
*_cv.pdf
*_cv.docx

# --- The virtual environment: each machine has its own, requirements.txt is enough.
.venv/

# --- Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# --- Temporary files
*.tmp
